<p>Russian President Vladimir Putin presided over a scaled-back Victory Day parade on Moscow’s Red Square on May 9, with heavy security and no tanks, missiles or other heavy weapons displayed on the square for the first time in nearly two decades. The event included a combat-jet flyover. Russian officials cited security conditions and the threat of Ukrainian attacks, while Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov said authorities had taken “additional security measures”. In his parade speech, Putin said Russian troops in Ukraine faced “an aggressive force that is armed and supported by the entire bloc of NATO” and said Russia’s goals were “just”. The parade took place during a U.S.-brokered three-day ceasefire that President Trump announced, with Moscow and Kyiv later accusing each other of violations. After the ceremony, Putin told reporters he believed the Ukraine conflict was “coming to an end,” criticized Western support for Kyiv and said he would meet Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy in a third country only after all conditions for a long-term peace agreement had been settled. He also said he would be willing to discuss new European security arrangements and named former German Chancellor Gerhard Schröder as his preferred interlocutor for talks with Europe.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/aq7LrLT9InpeLGMxCw2hRVlfwEn0dt-JImdc5hOgbAmIrKBFyNKun0nR2Cnp2AcdXC28HH2I199LWYJr5uEq1v4XatWBjQS7d6hEHBF3n7t8P30NgmcFJUE9-pQ7BBul5QiSPgePWCs0_TZWUVahGFNQBlCp_7HjbEFCKvSJCQjjOtugnlwq_hctxLebb3DcXqJZnWU-eRrf3kzGf_xxAmSE8lPRihOA14HMjaWG_ISzDpTpwC68ChZeWpK3NiIgsNJwYM6UUYxn8GCr2A' alt='Russian President Vladimir Putin speaks at the Victory Day military parade in Moscow on Saturday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Systems shown on screens: Russian state television and giant screens showed the Yars intercontinental ballistic missile, Peresvet laser weapon, S-500 air defense system, Su-57 fighter jets, drones and the Arkhangelsk nuclear submarine.</li><li>North Korean troops: North Korean soldiers joined the march after reports that Pyongyang’s troops had fought alongside Russian forces in the Kursk region.</li><li>Shorter event: The parade lasted about 45 minutes; NewsMaker reported that previous Victory Day parades usually ran at least an hour.</li><li>Limited guests: Foreign leader attendance was limited compared with previous Victory Day events, with several reports saying only a small group of Russia-aligned or friendly leaders attended.</li></ul><blockquote>Victory has always been and will be ours - Vladimir Putin</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Kremlin: Dmitry Peskov said there was still a “long road” to reaching a peace agreement on Ukraine, despite Putin’s suggestion that the war was moving toward an end. (<a href='https://www.lavanguardia.com/internacional/20260509/11534064/desfile-dia-victoria-moscu-imagenes.html'>La Vanguardia</a>)</li><li>Vladimir Putin: Putin argued that Western “globalist” elites were using Ukrainians as proxies and said Western expectations of a rapid Russian defeat or state collapse had failed. (<a href='https://www.newstalkzb.co.nz/news/world/putin-says-ukraine-war-is-winding-down-and-blasts-the-west-for-backing-kyiv/'>Newstalk ZB</a>, <a href='https://www.irishnews.com/news/world/tight-security-as-moscow-marks-victory-day-with-red-square-parade-DJR44TNAJJMV7FYL24DZA6CACU/'>Irish News</a>)</li><li>U.S. administration: Reports said Putin described the Trump administration as genuinely committed to finding a solution, even as the Kremlin said peace talks brokered by that administration were on pause. (<a href='https://www.rtp.pt/noticias/mundo/putin-disposto-a-reunir-se-com-zelensky-e-afirma-que-guerra-esta-a-chegar-ao-fim_n1740202'>RTP</a>, <a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458744/putin-says-he-thinks-russia-ukraine-war-is-coming-to-an-end'>Aaj TV</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/army-is-fighting-aggressive-nato-backed-force-in-v